&lt;h2&gt;About us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://constructorlabs.org/&quot;&gt;Constructor Labs&lt;/a&gt; is the research arm of Constructor Knowledge, based at Campus Ring 1 in Bremen, Germany. Our work is organized around three units: Knowledge Labs, Cyber Labs and Science Labs. We apply computing, software and robotics research to make scientists, teachers and students more effective, working with institutional partners that include CERN, NUS, Carnegie Mellon and Fraunhofer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://constructorlabs.org/solutions/edtech/&quot;&gt;EdTech practice&lt;/a&gt; produces research that runs in production. AI-supported remote proctoring is in use at the Irish Aviation Authority, Princess Nourah University and Saudi Electronic University, and our course delivery platform is used by CERN, EPFL, MariaDB and Acronis. For industry clients, we build tailored BSc, MSc and PhD pipelines, L&amp;amp;D operating models, AI upskilling programmes and customer training systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Constructor Labs Solutions (CLS)&lt;/strong&gt; is our client-facing systems integrator for the education and research sector, launching in

&lt;h3&gt;About the position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are expected to conduct and lead internationally competitive research in AI-driven semantic analysis and automated reasoning-flow modeling, with applications to educational materials, scientific documents, and research authoring. Your work will focus on developing advanced methods for semantic structure extraction, conceptual and argumentative flow reconstruction, rationale-aware content generation, metacognitive prompting, and adaptive personalization. Core research contributions will include designing algorithms for concept and structure extraction, building neural/graph hybrid models for pedagogical reasoning, implementing ontology-alignment methods for cross-domain transfer, and creating human-in-the-loop optimization pipelines that incorporate expert feedback—aligning with the multi-year research roadmap (WP1–WP3) .&lt;/p&gt;
